## Architecture Decision Records

This project uses **Architecture Decision Records (ADRs)** to document architectural decisions. For context and rationale, see [docs/adr/README.md](../docs/adr/README.md).

**Key ADRs:**
- [ADR-0002](../docs/adr/0002-use-page-object-pattern.md): Page Object Pattern
- [ADR-0003](../docs/adr/0003-separate-locators-from-page-objects.md): Separate Locators
- [ADR-0004](../docs/adr/0004-use-cy-session-for-login-persistence.md): Session Persistence
- [ADR-0005](../docs/adr/0005-use-allure-for-test-reporting.md): Allure Reporting
- [ADR-0006](../docs/adr/0006-mandatory-documentation-for-new-tests.md): Mandatory Documentation
- [ADR-0007](../docs/adr/0007-separate-specs-by-functionality-and-type.md): Separate Specs
- [ADR-0008](../docs/adr/0008-use-page-object-hierarchy.md): Page Object Hierarchy
- [ADR-0009](../docs/adr/0009-use-faker-for-dynamic-test-data.md): Faker for Dynamic Data
- [ADR-0010](../docs/adr/0010-use-tags-for-test-filtering.md): Tags for Test Filtering
- [ADR-0011](../docs/adr/0011-use-conditional-intercepts.md): Conditional Intercepts

---

## Directory Structure

- `cypress/e2e`: specifications organized by module. The `specPattern` in `cypress.config.js` ensures execution order. **See [ADR-0007](../docs/adr/0007-separate-specs-by-functionality-and-type.md)**
- `cypress/support/pages`: Page Object classes with interaction logic. **See [ADR-0002](../docs/adr/0002-use-page-object-pattern.md)** and [ADR-0008](../docs/adr/0008-use-page-object-hierarchy.md)
- `cypress/support/locators`: files that centralize selectors. **See [ADR-0003](../docs/adr/0003-separate-locators-from-page-objects.md)**
- `cypress/support/factory`: data factories built with Faker. **See [ADR-0009](../docs/adr/0009-use-faker-for-dynamic-test-data.md)**
- `cypress/support/commands.js`: utility commands (login, menu navigation, validations).
- `cypress/support/e2e.js`: loads plugins (Allure, cypress-xpath, Percy, cypress-grep) and global hooks.
- `cypress/fixtures`: static test data.
- `docs/cases/`: architecture documentation for each spec. **See [ADR-0006](../docs/adr/0006-mandatory-documentation-for-new-tests.md)**
- `allure-results` and `allure-report`: test reports. **See [ADR-0005](../docs/adr/0005-use-allure-for-test-reporting.md)**

---

## Main Configuration

- `cypress.config.js`: `baseUrl`, `viewport` 1366x768, `defaultCommandTimeout` 50s.
- `setupNodeEvents`: registers `allure-cypress` and `@cypress/grep`.
- `testIsolation: false` preserves states between tests.

---

## Execution Flows

**npm scripts:**
- `npm run e2e`: runs Cypress with Allure enabled
- `npm run test:chrome|test:firefox`: specific browser
- `npm run test:allure`: generates and opens Allure report
- `npm run lint`: validates ESLint standards

---

## Data Flow

- Use fixtures/factories for test data (Faker for dynamic values). **See [ADR-0009](../docs/adr/0009-use-faker-for-dynamic-test-data.md)**
- Use `cy.session` for login: **For fiscal functionalities** (NFe, NFCe, SPED, Sintegra), use `cy.login()` with fiscal user. **For other functionalities**, use `cy.loginArmazenandoSessao()` with default user. **See [ADR-0004](../docs/adr/0004-use-cy-session-for-login-persistence.md)**
- Global hooks in `support/e2e.js` intercept HTTP 500 errors. **See [ADR-0011](../docs/adr/0011-use-conditional-intercepts.md)** for conditional intercepts

---

## Reports and Evidence

- Allure reports: `npm run report:allure` generates HTML from `allure-results`. **See [ADR-0005](../docs/adr/0005-use-allure-for-test-reporting.md)**
- Screenshots: `cypress/screenshots` folder
- CI integration: `allure-results` can be published in pipelines

